,{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order (τ = n − α, Gallai), so the minimum cover avoiding the least vertex of a symmetric","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"difference. Every vertex with a self-loop is in it; parallel edges count once. The cost is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"maximumIndependentSet()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s: O(m √n) on bipartite components.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumvertexcover()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumVertexCover()","title":"minimumVertexCover()","type":"topic"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/maximumIndependentSet()":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"maximumIndependentSet"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximumIndependentSet()","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximumindependentset()","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A maximum independent set (exact): of all the largest ones, the lexicographically least by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex index, in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order; [] for the empty graph. Of two sets of one size, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lesser holds the least vertex of their symmetric difference (","type":"text"},{"code":"maximumClique()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s rule, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on a loop-free graph this is ","type":"text"},{"code":"maximumClique()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of the complement). A vertex with a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"self-loop is never in it; parallel edges count once.","type":"text"}],"title":"maximumIndependentSet()"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/minimumEdgeCover()":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumEdgeCover","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"text":"]?","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumEdgeCover()","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumedgecover()","title":"minimumEdgeCover()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A minimum edge cover (positions, ascending), or nil when some vertex has no edge: the edges of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximumMatching()"},{"type":"text","text":", then for each vertex still uncovered, in vertex order, its first edge in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" order (a self-loop covers its vertex). n − ν edges (Gallai)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O(n · m · log n)."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/approximateMinimumDominatingSet(weight:)-6gboe":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"approximateMinimumDominatingSet"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A dominating set of at most H(Δ + 1) times the least weight (Chvátal’s greedy set cover;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"NetworkX "},{"code":"min_weighted_dominating_set","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the same set): repeatedly the vertex with the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"weight per newly dominated vertex of its closed neighbourhood, the least vertex index on ties."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Ratios are compared exactly, by cross-multiplication. "},{"code":"weight","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is called once per vertex."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O((n + m) log n)."}],"url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/approximateminimumdominatingset(weight:)-6gboe","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/approximateMinimumDominatingSet(weight:)-6gboe","title":"approximateMinimumDominatingSet(weight:)","type":"topic"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Graph","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Graph"}],"abstract":[{"text":"An undirected graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of undirected edges","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"between them. Kept apart from ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": an undirected graph is not a symmetric directed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one, and no type is both. ","type":"text"},{"code":"directed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" views it as one when an algorithm needs arcs.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/maximalIndependentSet(containing:)":{"role":"symbol","title":"maximalIndependentSet(containing:)","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximalindependentset(containing:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"maximalIndependentSet"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"containing"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST","text":"Sequence"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":">) -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"]?"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A maximal independent set containing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"seeds"},{"type":"text","text":", which go in first, then each vertex in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximalIndependentSet()"},{"type":"text","text":"; nil when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"seeds"},{"type":"text","text":" is not an independent set"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(two are adjacent, or one has a self-loop). Repeats are one seed. O(n + m)."}],"kind":